   "target": "decibel_dex::extracted_base_math::compute_base_needed",
   "task_id": "BA-base-012",
   "why": "The contract cannot be stated from an invariant alone. Naming the accumulated value needs a recursive spec function, and ruling out a `u128` overflow of the accumulator before the assert needs a monotonicity lemma proved by recursive `apply` -- induction the solver does not perform. Omitting the lemma's `y <= len(sizes)` side condition, or instantiating it at one point instead of with `forall ... apply`, each fails with a distinct fast error. The accumulation is linear on purpose: the reference proves in 0.7s, so the reasoning is the difficulty rather than the solver time."
  },
