   "target": "decibel_dex::extracted_quote_math::compute_quote_needed",
   "task_id": "QT-quote-007",
   "why": "Floors each level independently before summing, so the result is sum(floor(p*s/m)) and not floor(sum(p*s)/m); the two differ whenever any level has a remainder. WP alone yields a vacuous ensures and four sathard aborts, so the loop invariant must be discovered. Its accumulation loop needs a recursive helper whose proof sits at the solver boundary: it was the only unscorable run of corpus-v3-pilot-002 at 90s and the false timeout of pilot-001 at 40s. Blocked: a complete contract needs a recursive spec function plus a monotonicity lemma, and the per-level `p * s / m` term makes the resulting proof nonlinear -- the replay reports ~117k quantifier instantiations and it does not discharge at any budget tried up to 240s. Kept as the record of why the selection criterion prefers linear accumulation; `BA-base-012` exercises the same reasoning in under a second."
  },
